      "approved": false,
      "findings": {
        "critical": 0,
        "major": 1,
        "minor": 0,
        "suggestion": 0
      },
      "summary": "The tests cover the named registry, federation, signing, and identity cases. The secret-output test can miss a storage key exposed through an existing output because it checks values only for recognizable text patterns.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "infra/terraform/tests/release-identity.tftest.hcl",
          "line": 420,
          "message": "AC RELEASE-ID-04 is not enforced for opaque credential values. Check the output expressions or otherwise make the test fail when an output exposes a credential-bearing resource attribute.",
          "confidence": 0.94,
          "category": "testing",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The output check scans evaluated values for recognizable text patterns, but does not verify that the existing app_sql_grant_statements and model_endpoint outputs avoid credential-bearing resource attributes.",
            "failureScenario": "If output.model_endpoint is changed to expose azurerm_storage_account.demo.primary_access_key, Terraform can return an opaque key value that contains none of the searched words. The output count remains four and the regex passes, so the test passes while an output exposes storage-key material, contrary to AC RELEASE-ID-04."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
